  "tagline": "Open-source JSON database that pushes live query results to apps through changefeeds.",
  "description": "RethinkDB is a distributed JSON document database whose signature feature is changefeeds: any query can be turned into a live stream of updates, so apps can react to changes without polling or a separate message bus. Its ReQL query language is embedded in host languages as chainable functions and supports joins, map-reduce and geospatial queries, and Raft handles automatic failover. The company behind it shut down in 2016 and the project now lives under the Linux Foundation as a community effort. The last release was 2.4.4 in December 2023. Commits still land, but there has been no feature work in years.",
